# Web UI standards (Vite + MUI)

**Apps:** `driver-web`, `customer-web`, `admin-panel`, `super-admin-panel`.

**NOT mobile Expo UI** — for that see `ui-mobile.mdc`. `driver-app` Expo web export is still mobile rules.

**International bar:** WCAG 2.2 **Level AA**, Material Design 3 **8px grid**, Apple HIG **44×44px** touch, ISO 9241-210 usability.

**Tokens per app:** `src/styles/palette.ts` + `src/styles/theme.ts`. Shared purple brand — keep in sync when changing brand colors. Super Admin uses the same PALETTE on a **dark purple shell** (not Cursor gray `#1e1e1e`).

**Verify before done:**

```bash
# driver-web / customer-web
npm run typecheck && npm run build && npm run lint

# admin-panel / super-admin-panel
npm run build && npm run lint
```

---

## 1. Breakpoints (all four apps)

From `theme.ts`:

| Key | min width | Device intent |
|-----|-----------|---------------|
| `xs` | 0 | Phone |
| `sm` | 768px | Tablet / large phone |
| `md` | 1024px | Desktop — sidebar/nav permanent |
| `lg` | 1280px | Wide desktop |
| `xl` | 1536px | Ultra-wide |

**Test every UI change at 375px (xs) and 1024px (md).**

Responsive pattern:

```tsx
sx={{
  px: { xs: 3, sm: 4 },      // 24 → 32px page gutter
  py: { xs: 3, sm: 4 },
  gap: { xs: 2, sm: 3 },
}}
```

---

## 2. Spacing scale (8px grid — mandatory)

MUI `sx` number **`n` = n × 8px**. Allowed values:

| Unit | px | Use |
|------|-----|-----|
| 0.5 | 4 | Tight icon gap |
| 1 | 8 | Inline spacing, between touch targets |
| 1.5 | 12 | Compact rows, chat gutters |
| 2 | 16 | Default `Stack spacing`, form fields |
| 3 | 24 | Page gutter mobile, section padding |
| 4 | 32 | Page gutter desktop, card padding |
| 5 | 40 | Large section gap |
| 6 | 48 | FAQ / marketing vertical rhythm |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — off-grid
<Stack spacing="17px" sx={{ mb: 22, px: 18 }}>

// ✅ GOOD
<Stack spacing={2} sx={{ mb: 3, px: { xs: 3, sm: 4 } }}>
```

**Viewport:** use `minHeight: '100dvh'` for full-screen shells (mobile browser chrome). Avoid `100vh` alone.

**Content width:** `Container maxWidth="sm"` (prose/FAQ), `"md"` (dashboard content). Line length ~45–75 chars: `maxWidth: '65ch'` on long text.

