## 3. Color tokens (`palette.ts`)

| Token | Hex | Role |
|-------|-----|------|
| `darkest` | `#2a1448` | Deep purple, header gradient end |
| `base` | `#401f68` | Brand purple dark |
| `mid` | `#7c5b9c` | Secondary purple |
| `light` | `#c3aee0` | Soft accent |
| `pale` | `#f3effa` | Page background (`background.default`) |
| `ink` | `#2b2630` | Primary text |
| `gray` | `#8b8792` | Secondary text — **check contrast** on `pale` |
| `border` | `#e6e1ee` | Dividers |

MUI theme also sets `primary.main: '#6c8aff'` — **legacy blue accent**. New work: prefer `PALETTE.base` / extend theme rather than a third accent.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Box sx={{ color: '#1a1f36', bgcolor: '#f3effa', borderColor: '#e6e1ee' }}>

// ✅ GOOD
import { PALETTE } from '../../styles/palette'
<Box sx={{ color: PALETTE.ink, bgcolor: PALETTE.pale, borderColor: PALETTE.border }}>
```

**Contrast (WCAG AA):** body text ≥ **4.5:1** on surface; large text (≥18px bold / ≥24px) ≥ **3:1**. Never convey state by color alone — add icon + text.

**Dark mode:** if implemented, switch MUI `palette.mode` — do not leave orphaned CSS vars in `index.css` unused by components.

